  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New:\n- ImfHeaderReader reads the header fields of an Internet message as zero-copy ImfHeaderFieldView values, with ImfOptions for bare line feeds, long lines, 8-bit headers and limits.\n- ImfEntityReader reads a whole Internet message as a stream of events, following multipart bodies and embedded messages, with raw byte ranges and optional transfer decoding.\n- Add ImfHeaderWriter and ImfEntityWriter, streaming writers of Internet messages.\n- Add typed Internet message addresses, groups, message IDs and keyword phrases (RFC 5322, RFC 6854).\n- Add ImfDateTime, a typed Internet message date-time that keeps an unknown offset and leap seconds (RFC 5322).\n- Decode and write RFC 2047 encoded words in Internet message display names, keywords, comments and unstructured fields.\n- Read and write the MIME header fields of Internet messages, with Content-Disposition and cid: URIs (RFC 2045, RFC 2183, RFC 2392, RFC 3282).\n- Add ImfMessage, ImfReader and ImfWriter, a message object model with the conformance checks of RFC 5322 §3.6.\n- Add the MIME entity tree of Internet messages, with decoded content, attachments, cid: lookup and ImfMessageBuilder.\n- Read and write MHTML files, with Content-Location, multipart/related roots and URLs resolved to their parts (RFC 2557, RFC 2387).\n- Read and write mbox files (RFC 4155), and make Internet message defaults follow the standards.\n- `ImfWriter` writes a message read from an mbox file with CRLF line breaks.\n- Read and write Apple Mail EMLX files, with their metadata and partial files.",
